//< An unclosed string is refused as a "string" at the point the characters run out
//<
//< Caution: **Do not take the `EXPECT-NOT` off.** Grammar-internal words in the list tell the user
//< to type what cannot be typed (track_token_fail in `kspeg/engine.kspls`). Piled at the token's
//< head, it reads "expecting an expression" at the opening quote, not naming what is unclosed.
// EXPECT: expected a string
// EXPECT-NOT: character class
fn main(): I32 {
  s: = "never closed;
  return 0;
}
